# Fluwy Framework Context

## What is Fluwy?

Fluwy (`@fluwy/ui`, v0.10.0) is a YAML-driven UI framework built on SvelteKit 5, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS v4. It enables developers to build web applications by defining pages, layouts, components, and behaviors using YAML configuration files instead of writing Svelte components directly.

## Technology Stack

- **Framework**: SvelteKit (Svelte 5) with TypeScript
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 with `tailwind-merge`
- **Build Tool**: Vite
- **Package Manager**: pnpm
- **UI Primitives**: bits-ui
- **Icons**: iconify-icon (browse at icones.js.org)
- **Markdown**: marked + highlight.js
- **YAML**: yaml package
- **Dates**: dayjs
- **Toasts**: svelte-sonner

## Project Structure

```
fluwy/
  app/                     # YAML configuration files
    pages/                 # Page definitions (filesystem-based routing)
    layouts/               # Reusable layout templates
    themes/                # Theme files (TailwindCSS classes)
  src/
    lib/                   # Core library
      core/
        app/               # Application class and YAML compilation
        context/           # Reactive state management (Svelte stores)
        operations/        # Built-in operations (HTTP, auth, nav, etc.)
        controls/          # Control flow (conditions, loops)
        router/            # Filesystem-based routing
        utils/             # Normalizers, parsers, helpers
        adapters/          # API adapters (Strapi, etc.)
      components/
        primitives/        # div, h1-h6, p, text, row, column, link, image, markdown, code, b
        controls/          # condition, for-each, loop
        layouts/           # page, header, sidebar, footer, container, menu_group, menu_item, spacer
        common/            # dialog, dropdown, tabs, icon, avatar, void
        displays/          # table, pagination, date, date_from_now, email, phone
        forms/             # button, input, form, checkbox
      plugins/             # Built-in plugins (payloadcms)
      sveltekit.ts         # SvelteKit integration
      tailwind/            # Tailwind CSS integration
    routes/
      [...path]/           # Catch-all SvelteKit route
  docs/                    # Markdown documentation (see docs/README.md)
  tests/                   # Unit and integration tests
  static/                  # Static assets
```

## Key Architecture Concepts

### YAML Page Structure
Every page file uses `---` to separate head (metadata) from body (content):
```yaml
layout: doc
theme: my-theme
server:
  load:
    data: https://api.example.com/resource
---
h1: Page Title
p: ${data.description}
```

### Component System
Components are registered by category in `src/lib/index.ts` via `createApp()`. PascalCase names are converted to snake_case for YAML usage. Every component has implicit `class` and `content` properties.

### Operations
Operations are functions executed in sequence on events (`on_click`, `on_submit`, etc.). Built-in operations: `get`, `post`, `put`, `delete`, `load`, `goto`, `set_auth_token`, `unset_auth_token`, `set_cookie`, `open_dialog`, `close_dialog`, `alert`, `notify`, `vars`, `log`, `sleep`, `if`, `abort`, `set_form_errors`, `clear_form_errors`.

### Context
The `Context` object is a reactive Svelte store available on both server and client. It stores route params (`params.*`), auth tokens, server-loaded data (`vars`), form state (`form.data`, `form.errors`, `form.submitting`), and operation results (`response.data`, `response.status`).

### Template Strings
Use `${variable.path}` syntax in YAML values to reference context data. Supports dot notation and bracket notation.

### Routing
Filesystem-based: `app/pages/index.yaml` -> `/`, `app/pages/users/[id]/index.yaml` -> `/users/:id`. Dynamic params via bracket notation.

### Theming
Theme files in `app/themes/*.yaml` contain TailwindCSS classes. Applied via `theme:` in page/layout head. Component `class` property has highest priority over theme.

### Plugins
Extend Fluwy with `Plugin` interface: `{ name, operations?, components?, plugins? }`. Registered via `app.plug()`. Namespaced access: `plugin_name.operation_name`.

## Key Source Files

- `src/lib/index.ts` - Main entry, `createApp()`, component registration
- `src/lib/core/app/index.ts` - `Application` class
- `src/lib/core/render.svelte` - Recursive component renderer
- `src/lib/core/router/route.ts` - Route resolution
- `src/lib/core/context/index.ts` - Context/state management
- `src/lib/core/operations/index.ts` - Operation system
- `src/lib/core/utils/normalizers/normalize-to-components.ts` - YAML normalization

## Conventions

- **File naming**: kebab-case for routes/files, snake_case for params
- **Component names**: PascalCase in TypeScript, snake_case in YAML
- **Operations**: snake_case names
- **Plugin names**: snake_case
- **Testing**: Vitest for unit tests, Playwright for integration
- **Server-side validations only**: No client-side form validation

